{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "fps": 30,
  "notes": "Cast-wide clip standard. Rotations are degrees in the character's own frame, so no rig axis convention is assumed: flex = top of the bone moves forward, turn = toward the character's left, tilt = top leans to the character's left, raise = outer end of a clavicle lifts, swing = bone end moves forward. Waves are amp * sin(2*pi*(t/period) + phase_deg). Body clips never animate neck or arms below the clavicle, so gesture clips (neck, arms) can play on top without fighting them.",
  "body_roles_reserved_for_gestures": ["neck", "upperarm_l", "upperarm_r", "lowerarm_l", "lowerarm_r", "hand_l", "hand_r"],
